# Everything ./setup.sh can install, for every engine, provider and workload
# choice. Source file for uv pip compile. Output: setup-lock.txt
#
# setup.sh installs only the packages a run selects, with setup-lock.txt as a
# hash-pinned constraints file, so every package it installs, direct or
# transitive, has an exact version and hash from this one resolution. A package
# added to setup.sh must be added here and the lock regenerated.
#
# The lock is universal: one file for Python 3.10 to 3.14 on Linux and macOS,
# with environment markers where a platform needs a different version. setup.sh
# installs wheels only, so a version is capped below where a supported platform
# has no wheel for it. To regenerate:
#   uv pip compile requirements/setup.in -o requirements/setup-lock.txt --universal --python-version 3.10 --generate-hashes --no-header --upgrade
#
-c ../requirements-lock.txt

# Always
pyyaml>=6.0.3
sqlparse>=0.5.0

